             subspace $M$ are studied by means of the variation principle
             $\delta (H)=0$. It is shown that, if the Hamiltonian $H$ has a
             normal constant of motion $\Lambda$ or a group $G=(g)$ of such
             constants, and if the subspace $M$ is stable under $\Lambda$ or
             the group $G=(g)$, then variational solutions $\Phi$ show exactly
             the same type of symmetry properties as the exact eigenfunctions},
  coden = {CHPLBC},
  issn = {0009-2614},
